<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "https://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LorvexCarPlay.entitlements
  PROVISIONING REQUIRED: This entitlement activates the CarPlay template
  application scene. Apple must approve it for the Lorvex iOS App ID
  (com.lorvex.apple) before this file has any effect at runtime.

  Steps to activate:
    1. Submit a CarPlay entitlement request through the form at
       developer.apple.com/contact/carplay.
    2. Once approved, merge the approved entitlement key into
       LorvexMobileApp.entitlements, OR set this file as the Code Signing
       Entitlements for the iOS app target in Xcode / XcodeGen.
    3. Rebuild and re-profile the app.

  Category: com.apple.developer.carplay-communication is Apple's messaging and
  VoIP category. Apple's CarPlay categories name no task list (driving task
  covers tasks that help with the drive itself), so approval is uncertain. If
  Apple approves a different category, replace the key below with the one it
  grants; an App ID holds one category.

  Until Apple grants the entitlement the CarPlay scene configuration in
  Info.plist is silently ignored. The code compiles and tests pass without it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- The messaging and VoIP category; replace it with the category Apple approves. -->
  <key>com.apple.developer.carplay-communication</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
